<div class="page-header">
  <div class="page-header__text">
    <h1>About the portal</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">
      An alumni tracking system and a community portal for the Department of Management
      Information Systems at Istanbul University, Faculty of Economics.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Two products in one</h2>
    <p>
      The portal serves two needs that are usually built separately, and treats them as one
      system:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>An alumni tracking system.</strong> A structured, institutional record of MIS
        graduates — who they are, how to reach them, and how their careers have progressed.
        This is the data the department needs for accreditation reports, curriculum planning,
        and demonstrating the outcomes of the programme.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>An alumni portal.</strong> A community hub where graduates find each other,
        read department news, and share career opportunities.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The two reinforce each other: the more useful the portal is to alumni, the better the
      data the department holds; the better the data, the more the department can offer back.
    </p>

    <h2>What is implemented today</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Alumni directory with full create, read, update, and delete on the web and over JSON.</li>
      <li>Announcements, published and managed by department staff.</li>
      <li>Job postings with applications tracked against each posting.</li>
      <li>Donations recorded against alumni, exposed through the JSON API.</li>
      <li>An OpenAPI specification served by Swagger UI at <a href="/api-docs">/api-docs</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What is not implemented yet</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Authentication and accounts — the portal is open on a trusted network for now.</li>
      <li>Events, mentorship matching, and fundraising campaigns.</li>
      <li>Profile privacy controls and verified membership.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Built with</h2>
    <p>
      Node.js and Express with server-rendered EJS views, MySQL for storage, and hand-written
      SQL migrations. The interface follows the design system in
      <a href="https://github.com/FlowConductor/Alumni/blob/main/DESIGN.md">DESIGN.md</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

